description: 'Implement cooperative preemption / yield injection (review 12_safety:
  a handler that never yields starves the scheduler — documented hazard in docs/concurrency.md
  line ~202 ''Every long-running handler must yield''; pthread_join hangs otherwise).
  Current state: grep shows zero preemption machinery in src/ or runtime/. Deliverable:
  compiler-inserted yield points (MIR pass inserting jinn_yield() calls at loop back-edges
  in coroutine/actor contexts — MIR optimization justified because LLVM cannot do
  this) with opt-out attribute, OR runtime timer-driven preemption; pick per design
  discussion. Definition of done: a tight-loop actor no longer starves sibling actors;
  test in tests/concurrency_shutdown.rs with two actors where one spins; docs updated
  to remove the must-yield footgun.'
